WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.879
Episode ten: no signal on site.

2
00:00:01.879 --> 00:00:07.032
The technician submits anyway, and the report is sent when the connection comes back.

3
00:00:07.385 --> 00:00:08.623
The connection drops.

4
00:00:08.623 --> 00:00:10.215
The bar at the top says so.

5
00:00:10.215 --> 00:00:12.633
The technician presses Submit for review.

6
00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:16.862
The status is Review, and the bar says one report is waiting to be sent.

7
00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:18.885
Now the connection comes back.

8
00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:23.118
Without anyone pressing anything, the report is sent and the bar disappears.

9
00:00:23.469 --> 00:00:24.890
In submit(), navigator.

10
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:25.878
onLine is false.

11
00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:27.608
So there is no point trying.

12
00:00:27.608 --> 00:00:29.956
It goes straight to queueSubmission().

13
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:32.467
The outbox is a store in IndexedDB.

14
00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:37.837
The request is saved exactly as it would have been sent: URL, method, headers and body.

15
00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.244
That is why requests are plain objects.

16
00:00:40.597 --> 00:00:44.667
When the browser fires its online event, OfflineSync wakes up.

17
00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:48.935
autoSync is on, and one report is pending, so it calls syncNow().

18
00:00:49.286 --> 00:00:52.490
It sends the waiting entries one by one, oldest first,

19
00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.575
so the CRM gets reports in the order they were made.

20
00:00:55.928 --> 00:00:56.236
Sent.

21
00:00:56.236 --> 00:00:58.519
The entry is removed from the outbox.

22
00:00:58.519 --> 00:01:03.206
If the server had answered 500 instead, isTemporaryFailure() would say true,

23
00:01:03.206 --> 00:01:06.229
and the entry would simply wait for the next try.

24
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.577
Here is the same flow as a diagram in the code guide: offline submit,

25
00:01:10.577 --> 00:01:13.821
the outbox, and the sync when the connection comes back.

26
00:01:14.172 --> 00:01:16.467
To try this yourself, open sample.

27
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:21.261
html, open DevTools, and set the same breakpoints in the Sources panel.

28
00:01:21.261 --> 00:01:24.029
Then do what we did, and step through it.
